  "problem": "Given that the random variable $X∼B(210,0.6),$ use the normal approximation to the binomial distribution to approximate $P(120<X\\le 140).$ Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.8\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1949\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1922\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1894\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.7\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2236\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2206\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2177\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2546\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2514\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2483\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.03\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.04\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.9\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9732\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9738\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9744\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,2.0\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.9788\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.